{% set local_problem %}
<p>Decatur's established neighborhoods are full of mature trees — beautiful, but brutal on gutters. The historic areas around Bank Street and downtown feature century-old oaks that drop massive amounts of leaves every fall. Pine trees throughout Morgan County shed needles year-round. And the areas near Point Mallard have dense tree coverage that keeps gutters constantly filling.</p>

<p>For many Decatur homeowners, gutter cleaning becomes a recurring chore — or a recurring expense. Professional cleaning costs $150-200 per visit, and most homes need it 3-4 times per year. That's $600-800 annually, which adds up to more than a quality gutter guard system would cost over time.</p>

<p>The bigger problem is what happens when gutters clog between cleanings. During Decatur's heavy rains, clogged gutters overflow — sending water cascading toward your foundation instead of away from it. With the Tennessee River's influence on local water tables, that overflow can quickly become a basement or crawlspace problem.</p>

<p>Gutter guards solve this permanently. The right system keeps debris out while allowing Decatur's 55+ inches of annual rainfall to flow freely. Install once, and the cleaning headache is over.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers that fit over or inside your gutters, allowing water to flow through while blocking leaves, pine needles, twigs, and other debris. Different types work better for different debris challenges.</p>

<p>Micro-mesh guards with tiny perforations excel at blocking fine debris like pine needles — common throughout Decatur. Screen guards handle larger oak and maple leaves effectively. Solid covers use surface tension to pull water into the gutter while debris slides off the edge.</p>

<p>For most Decatur homes, we recommend micro-mesh guards. They handle both fine and coarse debris, work well with the area's mix of pine and hardwood trees, and are tough enough to withstand heavy debris loads during storms. We'll assess your specific situation and recommend the right solution.</p>
{% endset %}

